{"name":"Solemn Silence","hex":"#d3d8d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"solemn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to religious ceremonies and rites;  religious in nature; sacred.","Characterized by or performed with appropriate or great ceremony or formality.\n\nDeeply serious and sombre; grave."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solemn"},{"term":"silence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The absence of any sound.","The act of refraining from speaking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (someone or something) silent.","To repress the expression of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silence","blocks":[{"text":"Silence is the absence of ambient audible sound, the emission of sounds of such low intensity that they do not draw attention to themselves, or the state of having ceased to produce sounds; this latter sense can be extended to apply to the cessation or absence of any form of communication, whether through speech or other medium. Remaining mute can be a symptom of mental illness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg/330px-Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silence","wikidata":"Q502261"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/500px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/1280px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraa